              "t": "urbem vidēre",
              "fromCell": "n/a",
              "teaches": "An infinitive cannot express purpose in Latin prose — that is an English habit. Latin uses ad + gerundive, causā + gerundive, ut + subjunctive, or the supine.",
              "checked": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
